 Orders_test;o;s;t;both
 o←Orders.Make 8
 8 ExpectEq≢o
 (⍳8)ExpectEq o.id
 ExpectTrue∧/o.region∊Orders.Regions
 (o.id)ExpectEq(Orders.Make 8).id                        ⍝ deterministic
 (9 10)ExpectEq(9 Orders.Make 2).id                      ⍝ numbering can continue

⍝ Running totals: adding in two batches = adding all at once
 s←Orders.Empty Orders.Add 4↑o
 s←s Orders.Add 4↓o
 both←Orders.Empty Orders.Add o
 s.orders ExpectEq both.orders
 s.revenue ExpectEq both.revenue
 8 ExpectEq+/s.orders
 (Orders.Cents+/o.(qty×price))ExpectNear+/s.revenue

 t←Orders.Table s
 ExpectTrue∧/2≥/t[;3]                                    ⍝ biggest revenue first
 (Orders.Empty Orders.Add ⍬).orders ExpectEq 0 0 0 0     ⍝ empty batch changes nothing
 8 ExpectEq(Orders.Summary s).orders

⍝ A summary (as published to Kafka and read back as JSON) restores the state
 s←Orders.FromSummary 0 ⎕JSON 1 ⎕JSON Orders.Summary both
 both.orders ExpectEq s.orders
 both.revenue ExpectEq s.revenue
